      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Lumber is the structural element responsible for nearly every type of residential home being built today. It is made from timber that has been cut into specific sizes and shapes, typically used for construction applications to frame residential houses and roof decking or subflooring. The most common types of lumber are pine (softwood) and oak (hardwood). It refers to wood that has been processed and cut into standardized sizes for construction purposes, typically sawn or planed and is commonly used in residential and commercial building projects.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "木材是当今建造的几乎所有类型住宅的结构元素。它是由切割成特定尺寸和形状的木材制成的，通常用于建造住宅、屋顶板或底层地板。最常见的木材类型是松木 (软木）和橡木（硬木）。它指的是经过加工和切割成标准尺寸用于建筑目的的木材，通常是锯木或刨木，通常用于住宅和商业建筑项目。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
